From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: free stale tiled render targets under critical memory pressure

The texture GC never freed GPU-written tiled images. A game that switches
render resolution keeps ~800 MB of the other size alive, and on a 2 GB GPU
the kernel then moves the live targets into GTT. Under critical pressure,
write such images back and free them once unused for 160+ frames.
---
diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/textureCache.cpp b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/textureCache.cpp
index caf0d2c2..e5124112 100644
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/textureCache.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/textureCache.cpp
@@ -2033,7 +2033,11 @@ void TextureCache::RunGarbageCollector() {
 			}
 			if (owner->IsGpuModified()) {
 				const bool safe = owner->SafeToDownload();
-				if (safe && owner->info.IsTiled()) {
+				// Tiled targets go back to guest memory only under critical pressure, when they
+				// have gone unused for 160+ frames. Games that switch render resolution leave
+				// hundreds of MB of the other size behind, which pushes the live targets out of
+				// VRAM on GPUs with little of it.
+				if (safe && owner->info.IsTiled() && !aggressive) {
 					continue;
 				}
 				if (safe && !pressured) {
